
Project 4: Network Reconnaissance Detection with Suricata

Project Overview

This project focused on building a small network security monitoring lab to understand how a Security Operations Center (SOC) analyst can detect network reconnaissance activity using an Intrusion Detection System (IDS).

I used Kali Linux to generate controlled network reconnaissance traffic with Nmap and Ubuntu Server as the monitoring system running Suricata.

The objective was to simulate an attacker performing a TCP SYN scan and then observe how Suricata detected and logged the activity.

This project helped me understand the relationship between:

Attacker activity → Network traffic → IDS detection rule → Alert → Log analysis → SOC investigation

Lab Environment

Virtual Machines

Kali Linux

Used as the simulated attacker/reconnaissance machine.

Purpose:
	*	Generate network reconnaissance traffic.
	*	Run Nmap.
	*	Perform TCP SYN scanning against the Ubuntu Server.

Ubuntu Server

Used as the monitoring/IDS machine.

Purpose:
